    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d272">

                <pb facs="0501" n="377" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg377"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.51 Refugee Settlement Commission/149</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The First Secretary of the British Embassy</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cecil</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Under
                        Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Phillips</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-10-29"><hi rendition="#italic">October 29,
                        1923</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Under-Secretary</hi>: On September 10th
                    you handed to Mr. Chilton an Aide-Mémoire, No. 868.48/575 explaining the views
                    of the United States Government in regard to the relief of refugees in
                    Greece.</p>
                <p>This was forwarded to the Foreign Office, who, in acknowledging its receipt,
                    write that the Treasury, to whom your Aide-Mémoire was communicated have replied
                    that they are unable to give any assurances as regards the efforts of voluntary
                    societies in Europe and that, anyhow, there can be no question of further
                    Government assistance.</p>
                <pb facs="0502" n="378" xml:id="pg378"/>
                <p>This information is very vague, but Mr. Chilton asked me to pass it on to you for
                    what it is worth.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Cecil</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
